    "QueryItem": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "description": "One item to look for, with every condition that applies to it (decisions IT-1, IT-3).\n\nAn item is complete on its own, so the same process can run once per item: conditions that the user\ngave for the whole query are copied into every item. `category` null = the user named no item to look\nfor (IT-6): every category minus `excluded_categories` (\"아우터는 빼고 블랙\" = 상의·하의·원피스 중 블랙).\n`excluded_categories` keeps the exclusion form (like gender, G-3); code never rewrites it into the\nremaining categories.\n\n`item_id` (decision IT-8, 2026-11-11): \"i1\", \"i2\", ... in `items` order, so a result produced for one\nitem (for example by a per-item Agent) can be joined back to it after the items are sent apart.",
      "properties": {
        "attributes": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/AttributeFilter"
        },
        "category": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "$ref": "#/$defs/CategoryRef"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "default": null
        },
        "excluded_categories": {
          "items": {
            "$ref": "#/$defs/CategoryRef"
          },
          "title": "Excluded Categories",
          "type": "array"
        },
        "gender": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/GenderFilter"
        },
        "item_id": {
          "pattern": "^i[1-9][0-9]*$",
          "title": "Item Id",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "unsupported": {
          "items": {
            "$ref": "#/$defs/UnsupportedCondition"
          },
          "title": "Unsupported",
          "type": "array"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "item_id",
        "category",
        "excluded_categories",
        "gender",
        "attributes",
        "unsupported"
      ],
      "title": "QueryItem",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "SeasonRequest": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "description": "Planning season. `default_next` = the user named none and code filled the next fashion season.",
